From: =?UTF-8?q?=C3=98yvind=20Harboe?= <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 07:43:58 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] flow: global_placement, global_route and repair_design take
 -options

With OpenROAD #11755's options structs (carried OpenROAD patch 0248) the
three commands take their settings as a dict. The flow's own settings for
global_placement and for the first global_route are built as a dict and
passed with -options; GLOBAL_PLACEMENT_ARGS and GLOBAL_ROUTE_ARGS follow
as the switches they are, and <COMMAND>_OPTIONS, a Tcl dict from the
design, goes last, so that a key in it decides.

repair_design runs in two stages and global_placement at two calls, and a
dict has no way to say which one a key is for. A key @<stage> or
@<stage>.<call> in <COMMAND>_OPTIONS holds a dict for that stage or call
alone (command_options, util.tcl).

The incremental routes take -allow_congestion when the first route did:
the flow looks the key up in GLOBAL_ROUTE_OPTIONS itself (options_value),
spelled dotted at the top level.

Not upstreamed: the OpenROAD RFC is open. Carried for the comparison with
ORFS #4771's command arguments grammar; not proposed for merge.
